{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795378609,"nonce":"0koHriyyjTzv6UM+ASHXTX1PHYE=","title":"Release tarballs ship the static runtime for the other desktop triples","message":"ash --build --target \u003ctriple\u003e looks for the runtime in \u003cash-directory\u003e/\u003ctriple\u003e/ (aot_link.rs), and release.yml fills that directory for Android and iOS only, from the android-assets and ios-assets jobs that run cargo rustc -p ash_std --target \u003ctriple\u003e --crate-type staticlib and hand the result to scripts/package_release.sh. A cross build to another desktop triple therefore has no runtime beside the binary and needs --runtime PATH.\n\nWanted by the hxn session, whose hxn package hl --target \u003ctriple\u003e passes only --target and the --native-lib archives: ship the runtime for the other macOS architecture in each macOS tarball (x86_64-apple-darwin on macos-aarch64, aarch64-apple-darwin on macos-x86_64), so --target works with no extra flag. A desktop-assets job of the same shape as ios-assets, staged into the same mobile-assets directory.\n\nLinux: the other architecture's runtime is possible with the cross gcc the test workflow already installs; not planned until asked. Windows: not planned.\n\nDepends on bc17ebc: a cross build with --native-lib archives needs the per-build static-natives decision before the runtime matters.","files":null}]}